RipsReferral_CollectReferrerFee
├── when referrer is zero address
│   └── it should return zero.
├── when referrer has a custom fee set
│   ├── it should return fee based on custom fee percent.
│   └── it should update only currMonthVolume.
├── when no referral tiers are configured and default fee is zero
│   ├── it should return zero.
│   └── it should update only currMonthVolume.
├── when default fee is set and referrer has no prior activity
│   ├── it should return fee based on default fee percent.
│   └── it should update only currMonthVolume.
├── when referrer current period volume crosses a tier threshold
│   ├── it should return fee based on default fee percent.
│   └── it should update only currMonthVolume.
├── when referrers previous period volume reached a tier threshold
│   ├── it should return fee based on active fee percent.
│   └── it should update referrerStats.
├── when active fee percent is below default fee percent
│   ├── it should return fee based on default fee percent.
│   └── it should update only currMonthVolume.
├── when a new period starts after a consecutive active period
│   └── it should update referrerStats.
├── when a new period starts after an inactive period gap
│   ├── it should update referrerStats.
│   └── it should reset active fee percent to zero.
└── when two referrers have independent period tracking
    ├── it should apply tier fee to referrer A after their period ends.
    └── it should apply default fee to referrer B whose period has not yet ended.
